ait, I'm still not seeing the per-agency breakdown for on/off budget. Let me look more carefully at the data.\n\nActually, maybe I should reconsider what \"total on-budget and off-budget outlays\" means in the context of this question. \n\nI'm seeing that the total outlays represent the combined on-budget and off-budget figures. The question seems to clarify that it wants the comprehensive total outlay amount. This suggests I should focus on the aggregate figure, which appears to be the primary representation in the available tables. The data doesn't provide a clear per-agency breakdown between on-budget and off-budget categories, so the total outlay is likely the most accurate approach.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_d551825968a741dfa839b4fc","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\n\n# Let's parse all the fiscal year data for Department of Commerce from both bulletins\n# First from 2024 bulletin (has 2020-2024)\n# Then from 2020 bulletin (has 2016-2019)\n\n# Load both JSON files\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2024_12.json') as f:\n    data2024 = json.load(f)\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2020_12.json') as f:\n    data2020 = json.load(f)\n\n# Find the Commerce data\ndef find_commerce_data(data):\n    results = []\n    for elem in data.get('document', {}).get('elements', []):\n        if elem.get('type') == 'table':\n            content = str(elem.get('content', ''))\n            if 'Department of Commerce' in content and 'outlay' in content.lower():\n                # Parse the fiscal year data\n                import re\n                # Look for pattern like | 2020 | ... | 15918 |\n                matches = re.findall(r'\\|\\s*202[0-9]\\s*\\|.*?\\|(\\d+)\\s*\\|', content)\n                for m in matches:\n                    print(f'Found: {m}')\n                print('---')\n                print(content[:2000])\n                print('===')\n                break\n\nfind_commerce_data(data2024)\nprint('\\\\n\\\\n')\nfind_commerce_data(data2020)\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
